**********Extracted claims**********

TrajSV is a trajectory-based framework for sports video representations.
TrajSV addresses issues found in existing sports analytics studies, including data unavailability, lack of an effective trajectory-based framework, and the requirement for sufficient supervision labels.
TrajSV comprises three components: data preprocessing, Clip Representation Network (CRNet), and Video Representation Network (VRNet).
The data preprocessing module within TrajSV extracts player and ball trajectories from sports broadcast videos.
CRNet utilizes a trajectory-enhanced Transformer module to learn clip representations based on trajectories.
VRNet learns video representations by aggregating clip representations and visual features with an encoder-decoder architecture.
A triple contrastive loss is introduced in TrajSV to optimize both video and clip representations in an unsupervised manner.
Experiments verify TrajSV's effectiveness across three types of sports: soccer, basketball, and volleyball.
Experiments verify TrajSV's effectiveness for three downstream applications: sports video retrieval, action spotting, and video captioning.
TrajSV achieves state-of-the-art performance in sports video retrieval.
TrajSV shows a nearly 70% improvement in sports video retrieval performance.
TrajSV outperforms baselines in action spotting.
TrajSV achieves state-of-the-art results in 9 out of 17 action categories for action spotting.
TrajSV demonstrates a nearly 20% improvement in video captioning.
