Few studies have explored a trajectory-based framework capable of supporting different downstream tasks.
Existing techniques often overlook the underlying structure and information embedded in trajectories.
TrajSV extracts spatio-temporal trajectories from raw sports broadcast videos, deriving both video-level and clip-level representations.
The representations derived by TrajSV support a variety of downstream tasks and can be fine-tuned.
Extracting trajectories embeds both spatial and temporal features of a sports game, providing a shared foundation for different tasks.
